MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The portable SSD offers a useful complement to my desktop external drive: moving files without carrying the larger drive.",
    "The Blink cameras build on my basic door alarms and work with my Alexa devices, while the HDMI switch could make using my Blu-ray player and Fire TV together more convenient."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Fire TV Stick repeats a need already covered by my recent 4K Max bundle. The larger Echo Show interests me, but recently getting a Show 5 and its stand makes another display less timely.",
    "The internal drives assume an upgrade project I have not shown a need for. Headphones, five short charging cables, and a separate microphone also lack a clear current purpose; my webcam already includes a microphone."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My storage purchases seem to have been taken as interest in any storage device, although portable external storage serves a different purpose from internal computer drives.",
    "My Alexa and computer accessory purchases seem to have been treated as reasons to want more related equipment, even when it duplicates something I recently acquired or adds a function I do not currently need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter because they can satisfy a need: the Fire TV bundle and Show 5 accessories make similar devices less useful to me right now.",
    "I am more interested in practical additions that help my existing equipment work together than upgrades requiring an unplanned installation or an unverified hardware fit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The suggestions recognized my interest in practical electronics and Alexa devices, but sometimes confused useful additions with duplicate equipment or unsupported upgrade needs."
}
